{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonIdempotentModifiedTrace","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.AdditiveResidualSimplex","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.IsospinMirrorInvariance"],"declarations":33,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.twoTerm_mirror_split_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.twoTerm_mirror_split_A3","kind":"theorem","line":364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L364-L377","doc":"**`A = 3` Two-Term Mirror Binding Splitting Theorem (`B(³H) - B(³He) = c_EM`)**:\nIn the two-term `A = 3` nuclear binding functional, the strong-exchange determinant\n`(isospinExchange mag s).det` and the GPMT 3-body core `B3_core` are identical for\n`³H = (p, n, n)` and its mirror `³He = (n, p, p)` and cancel completely in the mirror\ndifference `B(³H) - B(³He)`, leaving the pure inter-nucleon pairwise electromagnetic\ncoupling `c_EM`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.bindingTwoTermA3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.bindingTwoTermA3","kind":"def","line":356,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L356-L362","doc":"Two-term `A = 3` nuclear binding functional combining:\n1. Any strong binding functional `F_strong` of the isospin-signed exchange determinant\n   `(isospinExchange mag s).det` and the `A = 3` GPMT 3-body core `B3_core`, and\n2. The repulsive inter-nucleon pairwise electromagnetic interaction `-c_EM * pairChargeA3 qN`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.pairChargeA3_helium3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.pairChargeA3_helium3","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L350-L354","doc":"The inter-nucleon pairwise electromagnetic charge operator equals `1` on `³He = (n, p, p)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.pairChargeA3_triton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.pairChargeA3_triton","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L344-L348","doc":"The inter-nucleon pairwise electromagnetic charge operator vanishes on `³H = (p, n, n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.two_mul_helium3Charges_eq_one_add_helium3Isospin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.two_mul_helium3Charges_eq_one_add_helium3Isospin","kind":"theorem","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L338-L342","doc":"The helium-3 electric charge vector `helium3Charges` satisfies the Gell-Mann–Nishijima\nrelation `2 * q_i = 1 + s_i` with `helium3Isospin`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.two_mul_tritonCharges_eq_one_add_tritonIsospin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.two_mul_tritonCharges_eq_one_add_tritonIsospin","kind":"theorem","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L332-L336","doc":"The triton electric charge vector `tritonCharges` satisfies the Gell-Mann–Nishijima\nrelation `2 * q_i = 1 + s_i` with `tritonIsospin`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.helium3Isospin_eq_neg_tritonIsospin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.helium3Isospin_eq_neg_tritonIsospin","kind":"theorem","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L326-L330","doc":"`³He` is the exact global isospin mirror `s ↦ -s` of `³H`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.helium3Isospin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.helium3Isospin","kind":"def","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L323-L324","doc":"Nucleon isospin labels of helium-3 `³He = (n, p, p)`: `![-1, 1, 1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.tritonIsospin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.tritonIsospin","kind":"def","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L320-L321","doc":"Nucleon isospin labels of the triton `³H = (p, n, n)`: `![1, -1, -1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.helium3Charges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.helium3Charges","kind":"def","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L317-L318","doc":"Nucleon electric charges of helium-3 `³He = (n, p, p)`: `![0, 1, 1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.tritonCharges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.tritonCharges","kind":"def","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L314-L315","doc":"Nucleon electric charges of the triton `³H = (p, n, n)`: `![1, 0, 0]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.pairChargeA3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.pairChargeA3","kind":"def","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L306-L312","doc":"Electric charge projection `q(s) = (1 + s) / 2` in doubled units (`2 q(s) = 1 + s`),\nor direct nucleon electric charge tuple `(q₁, q₂, q₃) : Fin 3 → R`.\nFor a 3-nucleon system with nucleon charges `qN : Fin 3 → R`, the inter-nucleon\npairwise electromagnetic charge operator counts the proton-proton pairs:\n`pairChargeA3 qN = qN 0 * qN 1 + qN 0 * qN 2 + qN 1 * qN 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.simplex_gpmt_cumulants_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.simplex_gpmt_cumulants_real","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L284-L296","doc":"Over `ℝ`, the GPMT-weighted cumulants `(mu2GPMT q, mu3GPMT q, mu4GPMT q)` satisfy the\nexact coordination-simplex equations `simplexA2`, `simplexA3`, `simplexA4` of\n`QOU.MassTheory.AdditiveResidualSimplex` for the single-algebra GPMT stratum\n`m₂ = 0`, `m₃ = -dMod111 q`, `m₄ = 2 * dMod111 q`, and discharge the deuteron\nhypothesis `simplexA2 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.BextGPMT_values_and_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.BextGPMT_values_and_pos","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L257-L282","doc":"Concrete values and strict positivity of the GPMT-renormalized extensive cluster\nbinding at `A = 2, 3, 4` for all `q > 0`:\n* `BextGPMT q 2 = 0` (deuteron carries zero `≥ 3`-row cluster content),\n* `BextGPMT q 3 = -dMod111 q > 0` (`A = 3` triton/helium-3 core is strictly attractive),\n* `BextGPMT q 4 = -6 * dMod111 q = 6 * BextGPMT q 3 > 0` (`A = 4` alpha-particle core). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.BextGPMT_eq_dMod111_mul_Bext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.BextGPMT_eq_dMod111_mul_Bext","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L247-L255","doc":"Factorization `BextGPMT q A = dMod111 q * (Bext A : R)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.BextGPMT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.BextGPMT","kind":"def","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L242-L245","doc":"The GPMT-weighted extensive cluster functional `BextGPMT q A = dMod111 q * Bext A`\n(Reading Y of `ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant` renormalized by `dMod111 q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.gpmt_threeRow_cumulant_signs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.gpmt_threeRow_cumulant_signs","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L223-L240","doc":"**GPMT 3-Row Cumulant Sign-Window Inversion Theorem**:\nFor all `q > 0`, weighting the killed `≥ 3`-row stratum by its canonical GPMT modified\nquantum dimension `dMod111 q` preserves the exact 2-body deuteron zero (`mu2GPMT q = 0`)\nand **inverts** the unweighted `(-, +)` sign pattern (`forward_sign_window_opposite`)\ninto the physical `(+, -)` nuclear binding sign window:\n`0 < mu3GPMT q` (3-body attraction) and `mu4GPMT q < 0` (4-body saturation), with\n`mu4GPMT q = -2 * mu3GPMT q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.muGPMT_closed_forms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.muGPMT_closed_forms","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L211-L221","doc":"Explicit closed forms of `(mu2GPMT q, mu3GPMT q, mu4GPMT q)` in terms of `dMod111 q`:\n`mu2GPMT q = 0`, `mu3GPMT q = -dMod111 q`, `mu4GPMT q = 2 * dMod111 q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.muGPMT_eq_dMod111_mul_nu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.muGPMT_eq_dMod111_mul_nu","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L195-L209","doc":"Exact linearity of the Mayer cumulant inversion under GPMT renormalization:\n`mu2GPMT q = dMod111 q * nu2`, `mu3GPMT q = dMod111 q * nu3`, `mu4GPMT q = dMod111 q * nu4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.mu4GPMT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.mu4GPMT","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L190-L193","doc":"GPMT-weighted 4-body (tetrahedron) Mayer cumulant\n`μ₄^{\\mathrm{GPMT}}(q) = S_{\\mathrm{GPMT}}(4) - 6 · μ₂^{\\mathrm{GPMT}}(q) - 4 · μ₃^{\\mathrm{GPMT}}(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.mu3GPMT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.mu3GPMT","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L185-L188","doc":"GPMT-weighted 3-body (triangle) Mayer cumulant\n`μ₃^{\\mathrm{GPMT}}(q) = S_{\\mathrm{GPMT}}(3) - 3 · μ₂^{\\mathrm{GPMT}}(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.mu2GPMT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.mu2GPMT","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L181-L183","doc":"GPMT-weighted 2-body (edge) Mayer cumulant `μ₂^{\\mathrm{GPMT}}(q) = S_{\\mathrm{GPMT}}(2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.sRow3GPMT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.sRow3GPMT","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L175-L179","doc":"The GPMT-renormalized `≥ 3`-row single-algebra trace stratum at cluster size `A`:\nweights the combinatorial signed-Springer-dimension sum `sRow3 A` by the GPMT\nmodified quantum dimension `dMod111 q` of the killed 3-row ideal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.dMod111_eq_neg_inv_qInt2_mul_qInt3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.dMod111_eq_neg_inv_qInt2_mul_qInt3","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L150-L165","doc":"**Quantum-Integer Reciprocal Form of `dMod111`**:\nFor every `q ≠ 0`, the GPMT modified quantum dimension of the killed `(1^3)` sector\nequals `-1 / ([2]_q [3]_q)`. Thus `-dMod111 q = 1 / ([2]_q [3]_q) > 0` is the positive\nreciprocal of the symmetric quantum-integer product `[2]_q [3]_q`, while the minus sign\ncomes strictly from the orientation of the simple zero `(z - z_D)` relative to `(z - q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.qInt3_pos_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.qInt3_pos_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L145-L148","doc":"For all `q > 0`, `[3]_q = q^2 + 1 + q^{-2} > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.qInt2_pos_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.qInt2_pos_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L140-L143","doc":"For all `q > 0`, the symmetric quantum integers `[2]_q` and `[3]_q` are strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.qInt3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.qInt3","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L137-L138","doc":"Symmetric quantum integer `[3]_q = q^2 + 1 + q^{-2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.qInt2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.qInt2","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L134-L135","doc":"Symmetric quantum integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.dMod111_neg_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.dMod111_neg_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L122-L132","doc":"**Strict Negativity of the GPMT Modified Quantum Dimension `d_D(S^{(1^3)})`**:\nFor every `q > 0` in a linear ordered field `R`,\n`dMod111 q = -q^3 / ((q^2 + 1)(q^4 + q^2 + 1)) < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.zD_sub_self_neg_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.zD_sub_self_neg_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L116-L120","doc":"For all `q > 0`, `zD q - q < 0` (`zD q < q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.zD_sub_self_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.zD_sub_self_eq","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L104-L114","doc":"**Root Ordering Theorem (`z_D < q` for all `q > 0`)**:\nThe Convention-D Markov root `z_D = q^3 / (q^2 + 1)` lies strictly below the\nsymmetric `(3)` Markov root `z = q` for all `q > 0`, with exact gap\n`zD q - q = -q / (q^2 + 1) < 0`. This root ordering is the structural origin\nof the negative sign of the GPMT modified quantum dimension `d_D(S^{(1^3)})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.pow_four_add_sq_add_one_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.pow_four_add_sq_add_one_pos","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L98-L102","doc":"For any `q : R`, `q^4 + q^2 + 1` is strictly positive in a strict ordered field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.sq_add_one_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.sq_add_one_pos","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GPMTThreeRowCumulantBridge.lean#L94-L96","doc":"For any `q : R`, `q^2 + 1` is strictly positive in a strict ordered field. ","signatureChunk":0}]}